    "storyTitle": "The Grand Georgian Credenza Reimagined: RIVA 170 Twin-Vitrine Hospitality Suite",
    "storyLead": "There is an unmistakable sense of calm that classical symmetry brings to a large room. Spanning a full 170 centimetres in width, RIVA 170 takes its cue from the great eighteenth-century British breakfront dressers and dining room credenzas, reinterpreting them for contemporary home coffee and evening aperitif culture.",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "Walk into an open-plan kitchen-living room in a converted Surrey coach house or a wide lateral apartment in Kensington, and a small cabinet against a four-metre wall can easily look lost. Large rooms demand architectural weight and classical proportion. RIVA 170 delivers that presence through a balanced 40 + 90 + 40 centimetre triptych: a central vertically grooved arched barista alcove flanked on both left and right by identical floor-to-ceiling glazed display towers. The silhouette immediately anchors a dining wall, creating a dedicated destination for morning flat whites, afternoon Darjeeling service, and late-evening digestifs without requiring a costly structural builders’ alcove.",
      "The interplay of light and texture across this 170-centimetre expanse is extraordinarily rich. During daylight hours, the sand beige membrane finish reads as a tranquil, stone-inspired neutral that softens hard plaster walls; by dusk, a single gesture beneath the contactless hand-wave sensor transforms the entire piece into a warm architectural beacon. Light spills downward across the ribbed central arch whilst the twin glazed towers—each fitted with 6-millimetre tempered glass shelves—illuminate your collection of porcelain demitasse cups, coupe glasses, ceramic canisters, and art books from both sides. Because the twin 40-centimetre towers are engineered as independent modular columns coupled to the 90-centimetre centrepiece, the cabinet possesses true breakfront depth and structural rigidity.",
      "Storage capacity inside RIVA 170 rivals that of a fitted butler’s pantry. Across the suite, you command two full-height glazed display vitrines, two enclosed lower side cupboards, a concealed double-door overhead storage bay above the arch, a wide soft-close telescopic accessory drawer, and a double-door central base larder. That means every single piece of hospitality equipment in your household—from a twin-boiler espresso machine, precision grinder, and milk frother on the 43-centimetre-deep central deck to forty guests’ worth of glassware, table napkins, coffee pods, and reserve bottles below—lives in one coherent, dust-free sanctuary crafted from 18-millimetre Grade-A full MDF."
    ],
    "seoHighlights": [
      "Commanding 170 × 45 × 205 cm symmetrical three-module breakfront suite (40 cm left vitrine + 90 cm arched station + 40 cm right vitrine).",
      "Twin full-height glazed display towers with 6 mm tempered glass shelves and contactless hand-wave daylight LED lighting across the grooved arch.",
      "Pantry-grade storage capacity in 18 mm full-MDF construction with sand beige membrane finish, matt black cup ironmongery, and soft-close hardware."
    ],
