    "storyTitle": " Warmth & Quiet Opulence: ARCO DORE 170 in Matt White with Brushed Gold Ironmongery",
    "storyLead": "When a bright, white-panelled British kitchen or drawing room calls for a touch of jewellery rather than stark industrial contrast, hardware changes the entire emotional temperature of a piece. ARCO DORE 170 pairs our 170-centimetre arched twin-vitrine silhouette with warm brushed gold metal handles.",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "Walk through the finest residential refurbishments in Belgravia, Bath, or Harrogate and you will notice how designers soften crisp white joinery: they introduce unlacquered brass taps, warm veined Calacatta marble, and brushed gold cabinet ironmongery. ARCO DORE 170 captures this exact sensibility. Sharing the commanding 170 by 45 by 205 centimetre breakfront proportions of our flagship arched series, it replaces dark ironmongery with delicately curved, satin-brushed gold metal cup pulls and handles. Against the pure matt white 18-millimetre full-MDF fascia, those brushed gold accents catch the morning sun and the warm glow of the internal LEDs, lending the cabinet a refined, drawing-room elegance that feels closer to bespoke freestanding furniture than kitchen utility storage.",
      "The central 90-centimetre arched alcove acts as a curated stage for your daily brewing ritual. Framed by a finely ribbed vertical backboard and crowned by a classical radius arch, the worktop provides 56 centimetres of headroom—more than enough for a polished stainless-steel or brass-accented espresso machine, a conical burr grinder, and a porcelain pouring set. A simple wave of the hand activates the contactless daylight LED strip recessed beneath the arch, casting a gentle, shadow-free glow across the work surface while simultaneously illuminating the twin 40-centimetre glazed towers on either flank. Through the clear glass doors, 6-millimetre tempered glass shelves display gold-rimmed bone china, crystal coupes, and artisanal tea tins like objects in a private boutique.",
      "Behind its graceful exterior, ARCO DORE 170 is an unapologetic workhorse of domestic organisation. Crafted entirely from 18-millimetre Grade-A MDF—never chipboard—its modular three-unit architecture can be installed as a unified 170-centimetre suite or separated if your floorplan ever evolves. The full-width central soft-close drawer keeps barista tools, spoons, and pods effortlessly accessible, while the twin overhead doors above the arch and four panelled base doors below swallow up an astonishing volume of dry larder goods, spare table settings, and entertaining essentials."
    ],
