    "storyTitle": "Floor-to-Ceiling Smoked Glass Drama on the Left Wing: The Architectural Poise of CLARO 130 LEFT",
    "storyLead": "There is something undeniably captivating about a floor-to-ceiling column of illuminated dark smoked glass. CLARO 130 LEFT pairs our 90-centimetre handleless white barista station with a full-height 205-centimetre black-framed smoked glass display tower on the left flank.",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "In contemporary interior architecture, contrast and verticality are two of the most powerful tools for making a room feel taller and more expensive. Measuring 130 centimetres wide by 205 centimetres high, CLARO 130 LEFT uses both principles to dramatic effect. While the right-hand 90-centimetre module anchors the composition with a clean matt white drawer-and-cupboard base, a 65-centimetre-tall open machine bay, and a twin-door smoked glass top cabinet, the left-hand 40-centimetre column drops its black-framed smoked glass door all the way from the top cornice down to the plinth. The result is an unbroken five-tier vertical gallery of tinted glass and warm LED light that draws the eye effortlessly upward.",
      "Imagine walking into your kitchen-diner on a dark British winter afternoon or hosting friends on a Friday evening. With the main room lights turned low, the internal LED illumination of CLARO 130 LEFT transforms the left-hand smoked glass column and the upper right cabinet into an L-shaped architectural light sculpture. The dark tint of the tempered glass softens the LED glow, eliminating glare while turning every crystal tumbler, espresso demitasse, decanter, and stoneware jug on the five internal shelves into a museum-lit vignette. Because the open preparation worktop sits on the right side of the tall column, right-handed baristas enjoy complete freedom of movement when locking in a portafilter, steaming milk, or setting down a serving tray.",
      "Like every piece in the Cabivella UK flagship collection, CLARO 130 LEFT is built from 18-millimetre Grade-A full MDF throughout—never flimsy particleboard. Its handleless doors and full-width damped telescopic drawer maintain a razor-sharp architectural profile that wipes clean in seconds. Furthermore, because the 40-centimetre full-height smoked glass tower and the 90-centimetre barista station are constructed as independent, precision-coupled modules, you retain the flexibility to uncouple the tall glass vitrine and stand it separately as a matching drinks or porcelain column whenever your room layout requires."
    ],
