    "storyTitle": "Clean Horizon Lines & Concealed Lower Storage: VELA 130 RIGHT Half-Vitrine Suite",
    "storyLead": "Mirrored for rooms where the main workflow approaches from the left, VELA 130 RIGHT combines an open left-hand barista deck with a right-hand half-vitrine tower—giving you glowing smoked-glass display at eye level and generous solid-door storage beneath.",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "When designing joinery for a British kitchen-diner or utility-breakfast room, alignment is what separates bespoke architecture from ordinary furniture. VELA 130 RIGHT establishes a crisp horizontal horizon line right across its 130-centimetre span. On the left wing sits the 90-centimetre barista preparation module; on the right wing stands a 40-centimetre companion tower whose upper half is glazed in black-framed smoked glass and whose lower half is enclosed behind a flush, handleless matt white 18-millimetre MDF door. Because the open 86 by 43 centimetre worktop sits on the left side, anyone stepping across from an adjacent kitchen island or dining table can reach the espresso machine and central drawer without walking around the tall tower.",
      "Look at how the upper and lower zones work together. Across the top of VELA 130 RIGHT, three black-framed smoked glass doors—two above the central preparation bay and a taller three-shelf vitrine on the upper right column—create a continuous band of warm, LED-lit glass. Behind that dark tinted glass, your espresso cups, pour-over decanters, and crystal stemware catch the recessed warm lighting without ever collecting kitchen dust. Below the worktop datum line, however, everything is calm, flush, and solid matt white: a wide soft-close telescopic drawer for barista instruments and three enclosed lower cupboard doors that hide bulk groceries, cleaning supplies, and extra kitchen appliances completely out of sight.",
      "Crafted from 100% 18-millimetre Grade-A full MDF—with zero chipboard in either carcass or fascia—VELA 130 RIGHT is built to endure decades of daily steam and heavy storage loads. The 65-centimetre vertical clearance in the preparation bay accommodates tall bean-to-cup machines with ease, while the separable modular coupling between the 90-centimetre station and the 40-centimetre right tower makes delivery through narrow British hallways and staircase turns completely straightforward."
    ],
