    "storyTitle": "The Sand Beige & Smoked Glass Sanctuary: VELA 170 Twin Half-Vitrine Credenza",
    "storyLead": "Few material pairings in contemporary European joinery feel as effortlessly sophisticated as warm sand beige MDF and black-framed smoked glass. VELA 170 brings this coveted palette to a grand 170-centimetre twin half-vitrine hospitality credenza.",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "Step inside the showroom of any leading architectural kitchen studio in Chelsea or Mayfair today and you will see a clear shift away from stark clinical white towards warm, earthen neutrals paired with dark bronze or black-framed smoked glass. VELA 170 embodies this exact aesthetic. Spanning 170 centimetres in width and rising 205 centimetres in height, its entire 18-millimetre full-MDF carcass and lower handleless doors are finished in a tactile, calm sand beige—a shade that radiates organic warmth even under overcast British skies. Above the waist-high horizon line, four black-framed smoked glass doors—two flanking half-vitrines on the outer 40-centimetre towers and a twin-door bridge cabinet above the central barista bay—crown the piece in warm, LED-lit sophistication.",
      "The visual balance of VELA 170 is masterfully judged. Because the lower halves of both outer 40-centimetre towers and the central 90-centimetre base unit are enclosed by solid sand beige doors and a flush full-width drawer, the lower portion of the cabinet reads as a grounded, monolithic dining room sideboard. Above that solid base, the smoked glass upper cabinets and the 65-centimetre-high central preparation alcove introduce depth, reflection, and warm ambient light. When the internal LED illumination is switched on in the evening, the tinted glass glows like embers against the soft sand beige frame, showcasing your finest glassware and porcelain while keeping every practical grocery item hidden in the four solid cupboards below.",
      "Engineered as a three-module 40 + 90 + 40 centimetre system in 100% 18-millimetre Grade-A MDF, VELA 170 offers immense structural strength and layout versatility. You can install all three modules together as a seamless 170-centimetre hospitality wall, or position the twin 40-centimetre half-vitrine towers on either side of a chimney breast with the 90-centimetre coffee station at the centre. With damped telescopic drawer runners, soft-close hinges, and an 86 by 43 centimetre machine deck, it is a true centrepiece for refined British living."
    ],
    "seoHighlights": [
      "170 × 45 × 205 cm twin half-vitrine architectural suite in warm sand beige 18 mm full MDF with four LED-lit black-framed smoked glass upper doors.",
      "Monolithic handleless lower credenza (four solid sand beige cupboard doors + full-width damped drawer) keeps bulk kitchen storage completely concealed.",
      "65 cm tall central barista preparation bay (86 × 43 cm net worktop) and separable 40 + 90 + 40 cm modular full-MDF construction."
    ],
