    "storyTitle": "The Grand Timber & Smoked Glass Credenza: NATURA 170 Twin-Vitrine Barista Wall",
    "storyLead": "For open-plan British living spaces, barn conversions, and dining rooms that call for the warmth of natural timber on an architectural scale, NATURA 170 unites a 170-centimetre natural oak-grain full-MDF carcass with twin floor-to-ceiling black-framed smoked glass towers.",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "Large modern rooms—filled with plasterboard, expansive double glazing, and stone floor tiles—can easily feel cool and acoustically hard without the grounding presence of timber. Spanning a full 170 centimetres in width and rising 205 centimetres in height, NATURA 170 introduces an immediate sense of organic warmth and architectural permanence. Framed on both left and right wings by floor-to-ceiling 40-centimetre black-framed smoked glass display towers, and bridged across the top by a matching twin-door smoked glass cabinet, its central 90-centimetre barista station celebrates the rich, vertical grain of natural oak across 18-millimetre Grade-A full MDF.",
      "Switch on the integrated warm LED lighting and NATURA 170 becomes the undisputed evening heart of the home. Twelve individual smoked-glass display compartments—five in the left tower, five in the right tower, and two in the upper central bridge—glow with warm amber light against the oak-grained interior back panels. Whether you are pulling morning flat whites on a rainy Tuesday or serving single-malt whisky and espresso martinis to guests on Saturday night, the combination of tinted glass, matt black framing, and warm timber grain creates an atmosphere that no painted white cupboard could ever replicate.",
      "In daily family use, the practical capacity of NATURA 170 is immense. The central preparation bay gives you 86 centimetres of width, 43 centimetres of depth, and 65 centimetres of vertical headroom for a dual-boiler espresso machine, commercial grinder, and pouring kettle. Directly below, a wide handleless drawer on damped telescopic runners keeps all barista tools organised, while the twin solid oak-grain lower doors conceal bulky bags of beans, milk stocks, and serving dishes. Built in three precision-coupled 18-millimetre full-MDF modules (40 + 90 + 40 cm), the side towers can be installed flush or positioned independently across your room."
    ],
